● Both fixes are in and verified end-to-end.

  Fix 1 — one execution produces the whole document

  What was actually wrong. It wasn't a Streamlit rerun. The narrative generators lived in app.py and only the "Generate Report" button ever called them, so
  the API path never reached them at all:

  - docgen_api._build_rs used a hard-coded text_stub — Abstract/Objective/Background/Section-5-intro/Conclusion were simply never generated.
  - _build_deg_eg used meta.get("text_sections") or {} — same.
  - The empty title was a second, separate cause: RS read header["title"], which only app.py set; and EI's generate_document passed {"signatures": …} as the
    entire ref_structure, so generate_report.js received an empty meta — no title, no document no., no fishbone, no logo.

  What I changed. The narrative generators moved into the backend so the app and the API run the same code, and build_payload now calls them unconditionally
  with the just-built tables passed in as arguments:

  - residual_solvent.generate_rs_text_sections(header, parsed, calc, validation, claude_text=)
  - deg_eg.generate_deg_eg_text_sections(meta, composition, assessment, validation, claude_text=) (+ deg_eg_observations and the FDA high-risk tuples)
  - ei_core._auto_background() moved out of app.py, so EI's Background prose now matches the app
  - EI's cover page: _ei_ref_structure / _ei_title / fishbone / logo built in build_payload and consumed by generate_document

  New entry point: docgen_api.generate_report(doc_type, meta, files=…, filenames=…, excel_bytes=…) — contract check → convert annexures → tables → narrative
  → render → DOCX, with progress_cb scaled across all phases. A caller-supplied text_sections is merged on top of the generated one, never a precondition.

  Fix 2 — product name has one source

  resolve_product_identity and apply_product_identity are deleted; composition_identity_report is now composition_column_report and returns only the RF14
  self-test. require_product_name() raises MissingProductNameError when the field is missing, and passes a placeholder-looking value through verbatim with a
  log line. All 8 call sites removed across app.py and docgen_api.py; BE NOC's annexure-derived names (product_info, rld_utilization,
  innovator.generic_name, _derive_api_names) now read meta["product_name"] only.

  Two judgment calls worth flagging: I kept is_placeholder_name because injection_support._find_api_row uses it to skip token-matching on a meaningless name
  (not to substitute one); and in BE NOC I treated innovator.generic_name as a product name (now single-sourced) while leaving
  brand_name/manufacturer/strength sourced from the innovator's own documents.

